Deploy VM fro Qcow2 image

1. Download qcow2 image
root@rocky-linux10 opt]# wget https://dl.rockylinux.org/pub/rocky/10/images/x86_64/Rocky-10-GenericCloud-Base.latest.x86_64.qcow2

2. Step 1: Verify the QCOW2 image
# qemu-img info Rocky-10-GenericCloud-Base.latest.x86_64.qcow2
image: Rocky-10-GenericCloud-Base.latest.x86_64.qcow2
file format: qcow2
virtual size: 10 GiB (10737418240 bytes)
disk size: 520 MiB
cluster_size: 65536
Format specific information:
    compat: 1.1
    compression type: zlib
    lazy refcounts: false
    refcount bits: 16
    corrupt: false
    extended l2: false
Child node '/file':
    filename: Rocky-10-GenericCloud-Base.latest.x86_64.qcow2
    protocol type: file
    file length: 520 MiB (544997376 bytes)
    disk size: 520 MiB

3. Copy the image to the libvirt images directory
# cp Rocky-9.qcow2 /var/lib/libvirt/images/

4: Create the VM using virt-install
virt-install \
  --name rocky-node1 \
  --memory 12288 \
  --vcpus 12 \
  --disk path=/var/lib/libvirt/images/rocky1.qcow2,format=qcow2,bus=virtio \
  --import \
  --network network=default \
  --os-variant rocky10 \
  --graphics none \
  --cloud-init root-password-generate=off,root-password-file=/root/rootpw \
  --console pty,target_type=serial

5. Valiate VM
# virsh list --all
 Id   Name          State
-----------------------------
 2    rocky-node1   running



Explanation:

--import tells KVM that the OS is already installed in the QCOW2 image.
--disk points to the existing QCOW2 file.
--network bridge=br0 attaches the VM to the bridge (replace br0 with your bridge name, e.g., cloudbr0).
--graphics vnc enables VNC console acces

